      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226477/assets/b35bd1000242bcbc00fcd5e1cd04d8f3b13e563f2df72234b438827949ad4ef5.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Therefore\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that as $x$ decreases to $-\\infty ,$ the graph of the function moves closer to the horizontal asymptote $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, as $x$ approaches $-\\infty ,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches $2,$ and we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=2.\n$$",
